<%#
  Read-only per-hoojah vote distribution. Local: dist (a UserAnalytics::Distribution).

  The bar markup is copied — NOT shared — from hujahs/_vote_bars: that partial is
  welded to a button_to vote form, this one only reads. Extracting a common bar partial
  was considered and rejected in Slice 5 and again in Slice 9 Task 4.7: the seam is four
  lines of markup, and the shared version would have to carry a "with buttons / without
  buttons" flag through the one widget in the product that must never sprout a control
  it wasn't asked for. Below k=5 total votes the split is suppressed ("fewer than 5
  votes") instead of rendering the numbers — a privacy floor from Slice 5 (UserAnalytics::K),
  not styling. Do not soften the copy and do not make the branch conditional on anything.

  DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.7) —
  docs/design-system/components/analytics/DistributionBar.prompt.md ("read-only bars, no
  buttons") plus readme.md VISUAL FOUNDATIONS on bars: "8px tall rounded track `#e5e7eb`,
  stance-colored fill by %, percentage label right-aligned". The three rows already were
  that. The TRACK AND LABEL HALF of each row — the `flex-1 mx-3 h-2` track, its inner
  fill, and the `w-10 text-right` percentage — is byte-identical to `_vote_bars`' on
  purpose, and that half must stay so: it is one bar living in two files.

  The rest of the row is NOT identical, and a reader who "fixes" the difference would be
  writing a regression, not closing one. Two differences, both real: the row WRAPPER here
  is `mb-2` where `_vote_bars`' is `mb-3`, so the three stance rows sit 4px closer
  together in this widget than in the vote widget; and the leading `w-16` stance-NAME
  column here occupies the slot where the vote widget puts its 44px vote button, which
  this one may not have at all (DistributionBar.prompt.md: "read-only bars, no buttons").
  Only the middle of the row is shared, and only the middle of the row is pinned.

  What changed is the surface. It was a hand-written
  `rounded border border-gray-100 bg-white px-4 py-3`; it is now `ui/_card`, so the 4px
  rounding and the grey edge go and the card `shadow` arrives. This one IS a card, so
  Card.prompt.md's first line — "Never round a feed card" — is the rule for the rounding.
  The edge is a token question, not a rounding one: readme.md's VISUAL FOUNDATIONS assign
  the greys by job — "Tailwind grays for hairlines (`#f3f4f6`), field borders/tracks
  (`#e5e7eb`), hover fills (`#f9fafb`)" — so `#f3f4f6` is the HAIRLINE token, which
  `ui/_divider` spends INSIDE a surface. Drawn around the outside as a bounding edge it is
  off-token. (Note what is NOT claimed: the design system does not forbid rounding as
  such. It rounds dialogs `rounded-lg`, rounds menus, and ships a 4px `--radius` for small
  chrome.) The stack gap moves 12px → `mb-2` (8px), which is the DS's
  "Cards stack with 8px gaps on a white page" and what `hujahs/_hujah_card` already uses.
  `last:mb-0` stays: the row of cards is the last thing on the page and the trailing
  margin would double up against `main`'s `py-6`.

  `padded:` carries the padding and `class:` carries only margin — never both padding
  routes at once, per the same-family ordering trap documented on `ui/_card`.

  Stance names are interpolated into `text-` and `bg-`, which the Tailwind scanner cannot
  see; both prefixes over the stance trio are covered by the `@source inline(...)`
  safelist in app/assets/tailwind/application.css. A NEW interpolated prefix here means a
  new entry there.

  STACKED VARIANT (Hoojah 2026, Slice 2026 Phase 4.6) — mockup "Analytics · dashboard"
  ~lines 1495-1507, the "Top hoojah" card. `stacked: true` swaps the three ROW form above
  for a single `rounded-full` track split into three stance-coloured segments (width-%,
  `gap-0.5` between them) plus a stance-coloured legend line below. This is a distinct
  widget, not a restyle of the three-row form — the per-hoojah list keeps the row form
  byte-for-byte, per the file-level note above about not softening the k=5 branch or
  touching the pinned track/label markup. `heading:` is optional small print rendered
  above the claim body (the mockup's "Top hoojah" label) — nil renders nothing, same
  `local_assigns.fetch` idiom `shared/_screen_header` uses for its optional `back:`.
  Suppression still applies to the stacked form: a top hoojah under k=5 shows the same
  "fewer than 5 votes" line and no segments, exactly as the row form does — the privacy
  floor is a property of `dist`, not of which markup renders it.
%>
<%
  stacked = local_assigns.fetch(:stacked, false)
  heading = local_assigns.fetch(:heading, nil)
  rows = [["agree", dist.agree, dist.agree_pct],
    ["neutral", dist.neutral, dist.neutral_pct],
    ["disagree", dist.disagree, dist.disagree_pct]]
%>
<%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {padded: true, class: "mb-2 last:mb-0"} do %>
  <% if heading.present? %>
    <p class="text-xs font-bold text-ink-2 mb-1"><%= heading %></p>
  <% end %>
  <p class="text-sm text-black mb-2 line-clamp-2"><%= strip_tags(dist.body) %></p>
  <% if dist.suppressed? %>
    <p class="text-xs text-light-grey">fewer than 5 votes</p>
  <% elsif stacked %>
    <div class="flex h-3 rounded-full overflow-hidden gap-0.5">
      <% rows.each do |stance, _count, pct| %>
        <div class="bg-<%= stance %>" style="width: <%= pct %>%"></div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="flex justify-between mt-2">
      <% rows.each do |stance, _count, pct| %>
        <small class="text-xs font-bold text-<%= stance %>"><%= stance.capitalize %> <%= pct %>%</small>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <% rows.each do |stance, count, pct| %>
      <div class="flex items-center mb-2 last:mb-0">
        <small class="w-16 text-<%= stance %>"><%= stance.capitalize %></small>
        <div class="flex-1 mx-3 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded overflow-hidden">
          <div class="h-2 rounded bg-<%= stance %>" style="width: <%= pct %>%"></div>
        </div>
        <small class="w-10 text-right text-<%= stance %>"><%= pct %>%</small>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
